WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
All right.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:02.779
Let's get right into audience questions for
the week.

00:00:02.779 --> 00:00:06.640
The first one, I've gotten it from a bunch
of different people since the Corona virus

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.010
pandemic got going.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.660
The question is, is this bitcoins big opportunity?

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.400
Will the Corona virus recession lead to bitcoins?

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.120
Huge adoption and also valuation.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:25.700
So full disclosure, I've already said when
all of this started, one of the moves I made

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.440
was I did pick up some additional bitcoin
and I've had some for years that I've just

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.680
been holding.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:38.850
And my thought is maybe it's a hedge that
is not correlated to the broader market.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.930
So it's conceivable that it's a hedge.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:41.940
It may not be.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.510
And in fact, on some days that the stock market
has been down hugely.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.510
So has Bitcoin.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.140
So I have no special knowledge.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.979
I did that, but I'm clueless.

00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:51.229
I don't know what I'm doing.

00:00:51.229 --> 00:00:53.539
Here is my thought.

00:00:53.539 --> 00:01:01.319
What is it that would have to happen with
the dollar for a lot of people to go to Bitcoin

00:01:01.319 --> 00:01:03.899
who are not already in the space?

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:08.500
What would have to happen to the euro for
people to go into Bitcoin?

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:15.240
Because this really is is more a question
of currency than it is of recession.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.630
And why do I say that?

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:21.869
The reason I say that is you get the tech
adoption barriers aside.

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:27.020
Imagine that people just as easily and of
course, that that it's just not going to happen.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.899
But imagine that people much more easily could
get and use bitcoin so that it becomes more

00:01:32.899 --> 00:01:38.409
comparable to getting and using U.S. dollars
or euro or whatever your local currency is.

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:45.200
If you get the tech barriers out of the way,
people are only going to be looking to bitcoin

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:53.460
as a flight to safety if their country's currency
either becomes much more volatile so that

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.659
it matches or approximate the volatility of
bitcoin.

00:01:56.659 --> 00:02:02.260
Because remember, bitcoin is very volatile
and we've seen it in the last couple of years

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:07.590
be worth as much as nineteen thousand dollars
per coin at the end of 2017, early 2018.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.720
I believe it's been all the way down to five.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.600
That's a four X swing.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:18.110
U.S. dollar, of course, has fluctuations,
but they are far smaller than what we've seen

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.110
in Bitcoin.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:23.610
So one thing that would need to happen if
we solve the tech barriers to more people

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:29.570
getting involved with bitcoin is the volatility
of bitcoin would have to come down while the

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:32.040
volume volatility of the dollar goes up.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.790
That would be one thing.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:42.710
Secondly, there would have to be some real
evidence that aside from what your investment

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:49.900
choices are with dollars, that going to bitcoin
is going to be safer over the long term than

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.260
sticking with dollars.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.200
And this is more than just volatility.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:03:00.510
Only if there is a signal that the dollar
will not only be volatile but might really

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.960
lose so much value that your purchasing power
will be decreased.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.040
Would people be encouraged to go and move
money to bitcoin?

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.280
And in addition to that.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.920
If it's not going to be useful for buying
things that you need, particularly if the

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:21.570
corona virus pandemic extends and we have
supply chain interruptions that are not currently

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:26.290
expected, and we have difficulties obtaining
certain products simply with U.S. dollars

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.460
on Web sites like Target.com and Amazon, etc.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:34.460
I don't think that there is going to be a
wholesale move in the direction of Bitcoin.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:40.960
My sense is that the move to bitcoin, which
over the last couple of weeks has seen bitcoin

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.690
ascend in value and maybe by the time this
clip publishes that will have reversed.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:53.840
I think that it is a fraction of the population
around the world that has said, hey, if governments

00:03:53.840 --> 00:04:00.840
can be really poor at dealing with the pandemic,
maybe I shouldn't be all in with their currency

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.010
either.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.340
And I'll pick up some bitcoin.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:09.200
I believe that that is the lion's share of
the move to bitcoin that we have seen over

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.850
the last month or so.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:16.160
If people really were saying, I've got to
get out of my state's kirp my country's currency

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.150
and get over to Bitcoin.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:23.780
You would have seen such a larger increase
in the value of Bitcoin than the one that

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.780
we've seen.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.720
So that's that's my view.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:33.190
Volatility would have to go up drastically
for government backed currencies, down for

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.190
bitcoin.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.620
The technical barriers would have to be solved.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:41.460
The corona virus situation would really have
to extend longer than even the best models

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.490
now suggest it would.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:48.240
And then in that case, yes, maybe this will
prove to be Bitcoin's big opportunity.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.780
If you disagree with me, let me know.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.690
That's what I'm seeing so far.

